[[Rey Skywalker|Rey's]] '''hut''' was a gray [[stone]] hut, made of several pieces of rock, located in the [[Jedi village]] on [[Temple Island]] on the [[planet]] [[Ahch-To]]. The hut served as a home of [[Force-sensitive]] [[scavenger]] Rey during her [[Jedi training]].

==Description==
The hut was a gray [[stone]] hut, made of several pieces of rock, located in the [[Jedi village]] on [[Temple Island]] on the [[Unknown Regions]] [[planet]] of [[Ahch-To]].<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref> The hut housed a stone bench and had a narrow window.<ref name="Expanded Edition" />

==History==
===Rey's training===
{{Quote|I&hellip; was cleaning my blaster. It went off.|Rey|<ref name="Expanded Edition" />}}
When Rey arrived on the [[Temple Island]] to try to convince [[Luke Skywalker]] to become her [[Jedi Master]], he gave her one of the uninhabited huts in the [[Jedi village]].<ref name="Exegol">{{EncyclopediaCite|Exegol, the Unknown Regions and Wild Space}}</ref> On the first day of her training with Skywalker, Rey awoke to find [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] sitting across from her. She instinctively aimed her blaster at him and fired, only to blow a hole through her stone hut.<ref name="Expanded Edition" />

[[File:Luke_interrupting_Rey_and_Kylo_Ren.png|thumb|left|266px|Disillusioned by Skywalker's rejection of the Jedi legacy, Rey turned to Kylo Ren, with whom she could communicate across the stars.]]
After Rey had failed to find the answers to the identities of her parents in the [[Mirror cave]], she turned to the one person whom she felt could relate to her sense of solitude and loss: [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]]. He listened intently as Rey recalled her experience in the [[cave]], and he insisted she was not alone despite her sense of loneliness. Rey returned his gesture, in kind, and came to hope that it was not too late for him to return to the light.<ref name="Expanded Edition" /> By then, their bond had reached an unprecedented level in strength and raw power<ref name="TLJ:TVD">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> to the extent that Rey compared it to touching a live wire. She tentatively raised her hand to touch him, although she expected their hands to simply pass through each other. When their fingers actually touched, Rey gasped and grasped Ren's hand. At that moment, however, Skywalker&mdash;now reconnected with the Force and planning to return with her&mdash;witnessed their bond with his own eyes,<ref name="Expanded Edition" /> and thought that they were in league. Luke had gestured at the walls and the ceiling of the hut, and all the stone blocks were shot outward<ref name="Last Jedi Junior">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: A Junior Novel]]''</ref> from the hut's center, scattering them around the bench.<ref name="Expanded Edition" /> Having decided that Rey could not be trusted anymore, Skywalker ordered her to leave the planet.<ref name="Last Jedi Junior" />

===Legacy===
After Rey's departure and Skywalker's [[death]], the [[Clan Matron]] [[Alcida-Auka]] turned her mind towards the many things that needed fixing in their aftermath, including that Rey's hut needed rebuilding.<ref name="Expanded Edition" />

